WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.238
Step five reads one payload in full:
the Azure retirement from Module 1.

2
00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:09.199
It's a create, keyed on Azure
and the notice's tracking I D.

3
00:00:09.199 --> 00:00:15.100
Its severity is P3, with a response window
of eighty-six thousand four hundred

4
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.128
seconds, twenty-four hours,

5
00:00:17.128 --> 00:00:21.737
so the response is due November
tenth, 2026, a day after the run.

6
00:00:21.737 --> 00:00:24.406
The retirement date is kept apart,

7
00:00:24.406 --> 00:00:28.313
in the action due field:
September thirtieth, 2027.

8
00:00:28.313 --> 00:00:29.262
Both are right.

9
00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.672
The owner picks the task up within a day,

10
00:00:31.672 --> 00:00:35.287
and the work is due by the
retirement date, ten months later.

11
00:00:35.287 --> 00:00:41.359
It goes to cloud platform engineering,
with the contingency review flag set,

12
00:00:41.359 --> 00:00:45.213
and it supports C M three, C
M four, C P two and S I five.

13
00:00:45.213 --> 00:00:49.153
And the Ticket-to-Machine block
puts it in the Human decision lane,

14
00:00:49.153 --> 00:00:53.896
with the system owner as approver, and a
re-read check: the next collection shows

15
00:00:53.896 --> 00:00:58.780
the notice closed or no longer listed, or
the named resources no longer affected.
